\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{What this draft claims and proposes}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{research-programme}

\p{The architecture, probability, optimization, and control definitions in
this draft are taken from named sources or stated as standard specializations.
The note uses them to describe contemporary post-training protocols in one
notation.}

\p{Several later objects are original research interfaces. The lifecycle cost
vector, trust contract, costed potential, and acquisition witness are marked
as FTIP proposals in their own trees. They organize questions; they are not
results of the cited literature.}

\p{The first complete draft should make every symbol traceable to a prior
definition and every imported claim traceable to a source. The next draft can
then state candidate theorems with explicit assumptions. A theorem card will
be added only when its hypotheses and counterexamples can be read without
guessing which protocol or cost is meant.}
